  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through next Sunday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Strong upper level ridging remains the\ndominant feature across northern and central Nevada. An upper\nlevel trough will skirt across southern Canada and the Pacific\nNorthwest today, resulting in breezy to locally windy conditions \nacross northern and central Nevada, along with a couple to a few \ndegrees of cooling. The upper ridge over the Great Basin region \nwill be further suppressed southward on Monday, with an additional\ncouple to few degrees of cooling across the region, with continued\ndry conditions. Temperatures begin to trend warmer on Tuesday. \nIncreasing confidence in above normal temperatures later this \nweek as high pressure builds across the entire Southwestern US. \nECMWF extreme forecast index is highlighting the northeastern \nportion of Nevada as an area that could see well above normal \ntemperatures Thursday through at least Saturday. The GFS model is \nin alignment with increasing high pressure for NV with 500mb \nheights reaching 600DAM across central NV on Friday. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: No changes to the NBM guidance.\nModerate to high confidence in increased winds this afternoon \nwith gusts of 30 to 40 mph across portions of northeastern Elko \nCounty. High confidence in Red Flag Warning conditions this \nafternoon and evening across fire weather zone 470. Increasing\nconfidence in near-record to record high temperatures Thursday\nthrough Saturday.",
